# The build context for the two REACTOR-ROOT images — orchestrator/Dockerfile and runner/Dockerfile,
# both of which are built with `context: ..` because their modules resolve `tech.mikhailov.fsm:engine`
# from the reactor. Those builds COPY named poms and named src/ trees, so nothing here changes what ends
# up in an image; what it changes is how much of this worktree is shipped to the daemon first. Without
# it that is ~130 MB of build output, differential-harness fixtures and node_modules per build, which is
# most of the wall clock of an otherwise cached build.
#
# engine/.dockerignore stays where it is: `engine` is built with `context: ../engine`, so this file is
# not consulted for it. It also records the sharper reason for the first rule below — a copied `target/`
# would let a stale jar, compiled by whatever JDK the developer happens to have, win over the one the
# image builds from source.
**/target/

# Differential-harness OUTPUT: the unpacked copies of the frozen corpora, tens of megabytes, rebuilt by
# `node harness/js-side.cjs`. Nothing reads them but a person.
#
# NOT harness/fixtures/ — those are the frozen JavaScript answers themselves, they are committed, and
# the harness TESTS read them during `mvn package` inside the image build. Excluding them here would
# fail every image build with a missing-fixture error, which is the one failure mode a .dockerignore is
# worst at explaining. harness/report.txt and harness/README.md are committed and are not output either.
**/harness/out/

# Node dependencies and stale Python bytecode. The n8n generator tree that these also covered
# (n8n/agentic/coverage/, n8n/agentic/reports/) is deleted; the two rules went with it rather than
# being left as paths that match nothing. What remains is named narrowly for a reason: a wildcard as
# broad as `**/coverage/` would one day match a directory inside a module's src/ tree and silently
# drop it from an image, which is the failure mode a .dockerignore is worst at showing you.
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/

# Live state, not source: n8n's sqlite database and Data Tables, and the orchestrator's default-path H2
# store from a `mvn spring-boot:run` in that directory. (The directory is `deploy/` now; `n8n-data` is
# the basename n8n itself used, so it stays.)
deploy/n8n-data/
orchestrator/data/
**/*.mv.db
**/*.trace.db
**/*.lock.db

# Never part of a build, and .git in particular carries the full history into every context.
.git/
**/.idea/
**/*.iml
